    {
      "name": "replay_first_pick",
      "description": "Backtest the first pump.fun pick on the bonding curve or PumpSwap for free and see the price after the bot's own delay, the effect of its own order, every fee, the result in SOL beside the simplest paper trade, or the reason the order would have failed. With a landing rate and sample size or a send log it also estimates cash and the chance of still holding tokens. In this example the chain recorded two transactions in the same second and one of them failed. The send times and the two missed orders are made up to show what a bot could supply. Two of four sends landed and the estimated delays run from one to two seconds with a middle value of 1.5 seconds. On the recorded trades the 0.1 SOL pick would have lost 0.002522473 SOL if both orders landed. With half of sends landing independently, the buy misses half the time and the buy fills but the sale misses a quarter of the time. The estimated change in cash is −0.02563061825 SOL, with a range of about −0.025647 to −0.012810 SOL from uncertainty in four sends. The open tokens are reported separately because the bot has received no SOL for them. This is the free sample, allowed 6 times an hour for a caller with an exit window of up to 15 minutes, and it leaves the other picks of the document out.",
